% Vacuum Erection Devices (VED): LCD L34824 and its Policy Article A52712
% (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and decides
% the claims for a vacuum erection device (L7900) and its related accessories
% (L7902) — by concluding NOTHING about them. The LCD states no coverage
% criteria: "Vacuum erection devices (L7900) and related accessories (L7902)
% are statutorily non-covered (see related Policy Article for additional
% details)"; and the Policy Article gives the reason: "Vacuum erection
% devices (L7900) and related supplies are considered Prosthetic Devices
% under the Prosthetic Devices benefit category (Social Security Act
% §1861(s)(8)). For dates of service on or after July 1, 2015, codes L7900
% and L7902 are statutorily non-covered based on the Achieving a Better Life
% Experience (ABLE) Act of 2014 (see Social Security Act 1834(a)(1)(I))."
%
% How this is read. The codes are within the scope of the model (a claim for
% them is decided, not left unread), but no rule places them in a benefit
% category — the statute takes them out of the prosthetic devices benefit
% the article names — and no rule makes a claim for them reasonable and
% necessary: the LCD's coverage section has no criterion to encode. Every
% claim fails at applicability. The criteria of the period before 1 July
% 2015 are not in the current LCD text and are not modelled: a claim of that
% period concludes nothing too, for want of a text to cite.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base vacuum erection includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base vacuum erection includes:

LCD L34824 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=34824".
the text of LCD L34824 is at "sources/lcd/L34824.txt".
Policy Article A52712 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52712".
the text of Policy Article A52712 is at "sources/article/A52712.txt".

section applicability is:

vacuum_erection has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the device and its accessories. No benefit
% rule follows: "For dates of service on or after July 1, 2015, codes L7900
% and L7902 are statutorily non-covered based on the Achieving a Better Life
% Experience (ABLE) Act of 2014" (Policy Article A52712).
rule ved_codes with provenance LCD L34824,
        confer "Vacuum erection devices (L7900) and related accessories (L7902) are statutorily non-covered":
the policy for code a code is vacuum_erection
    if the code is in ["L7900", "L7902"].

section question is:

% No rule concludes that a claim for L7900 or L7902 is reasonable and
% necessary: the LCD's "Coverage Indications, Limitations and/or Medical
% Necessity" states only that the codes are statutorily non-covered.
